{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1041","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1041","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1041\",\"parent_revision\":\"3fc57dfca4a2f45f2b8a62e454e06aea135d2b82\",\"root_revision\":\"943e67d08755e8856d301e570bed63dd7650bc9dfe09937bdc16a07da666832f\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nAdd token usage visibility infrastructure so progressive disclosure improvements are measurable.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAssessment date: 2026-04-23\\n\\n| # | Condition | Status | Source |\\n|---|-----------|--------|--------|\\n| 1 | PostToolUse hook event format and available fields | AVAILABLE | `.claude/hooks/` existing hooks as reference |\\n| 2 | Token count field in Claude Code tool responses | DERIVABLE | Check if `usage` field appears in PostToolUse event payload |\\n| 3 | Log file location convention | AVAILABLE | `.claude/logs/` or `.tmp/logs/` |\\n| 4 | Whether Claude Code tool responses actually include token counts | MISSING | Must be verified empirically |\\n\\nVerdict: READY with one empirical verification needed (token field availability in PostToolUse payload). Implement hook first; report script second.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **token visibility: posttooluse logging hook + reporting script** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session 2026-03-24 \u2014 token efficiency plan for development-harness\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-24\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-23)\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\nP1 Feature. Additive only. Hook failure is non-blocking. Low risk.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- A PostToolUse hook in `.claude/hooks/` captures tool call metadata including token counts when available in the tool response\\n- Hook appends a JSONL entry per tool call to a log file at `.claude/logs/token-usage.jsonl` (or configurable path)\\n- A reporting script `scripts/token_usage_report.py` reads the log and produces: total tokens per session, per-tool breakdown, and a trend chart if matplotlib is available\\n- Hook written in JavaScript (Node.js) following the `.claude/hooks/` pattern\\n- Reporting script follows PEP 723 with `uv run` execution\\n- Log file is gitignored\\n- Regression: hook failure does not block the primary tool call (errors written to stderr only)\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `.claude/hooks/token-usage-logger.cjs` \u2014 new PostToolUse hook\\n- `.claude/hooks/hooks.json` \u2014 register new hook\\n- `scripts/token_usage_report.py` \u2014 new PEP 723 reporting script\\n- `.gitignore` \u2014 add `.claude/logs/`\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs a developer working on progressive disclosure improvements, I need a PostToolUse logging hook and reporting script to capture token usage data so I can measure whether context optimization changes actually reduce token consumption.\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nNo mechanism exists to measure token costs by workflow step. Optimizations (e.g., sam_ready progressive disclosure) are made blind with no before/after comparison.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n### 1. PostToolUse hook \u2014 `.claude/hooks/token-tracker.cjs`\\nIntercepts every MCP tool call result and logs response size metadata to a JSONL file.\\n\\nLog destination: `.claude/token-tracking/YYYY-MM-DD.jsonl` (project-local)\\n\\nJSONL record per tool call:\\n- `ts` \u2014 ISO timestamp\\n- `tool` \u2014 tool name (e.g., `mcp__plugin_dh_sam__sam_ready`)\\n- `session_id` \u2014 from hook env\\n- `response_bytes` \u2014 byte length of JSON-serialized response\\n- `response_tokens_est` \u2014 estimated tokens (bytes / 4)\\n\\nOnly log MCP tool calls (tool name starts with `mcp__`). Skip built-in tools.\\n\\nWire into `.claude/settings.json` PostToolUse hooks section.\\n\\n### 2. Reporting script \u2014 `scripts/token_usage_report.py`\\nPython CLI (typer + rich) that reads the JSONL logs and produces:\\n- Per-tool totals: call count, total bytes, total estimated tokens, average per call\\n- Top 10 most expensive single calls\\n- Per-session breakdown\\n- Date range filter flag\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"3f5ec36f6965468f05d9e0013071dfe9a55de78cbbb795e9e7ea3a6a80c3f7a8\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPvcVwg\"}"}